mpeg12dec reads a picture's A53 caption user data into a53_buf_ref before
its slices, and only mpeg_field_start() hands the buffer to a frame. Pictures
the decoder skips (open-GOP B-frames without a reference, P-frames before the
first I-frame, and anything dropped by -skip_frame) never get there, so their
captions stay in the buffer and the next decoded frame gets all of them.

A stream that starts mid-GOP, like a tuned-in broadcast, puts every caption
before its first I-frame on that frame, often hundreds of cc triplets. The
encoders write cc_count in 5 bits, so the SEI is malformed, and h264_vaapi
fails outright when it no longer fits the packed header:

  [h264_vaapi] Access unit too large: 8192 < 14608.
  [h264_vaapi] Failed to write extra header 0: -28.

Drop the buffered captions when a picture is skipped. They are not cleared
at the picture start code, because DVD-style captions are GOP user data that
comes before the picture header they belong to.

diff --git a/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c b/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
--- a/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mpeg12dec.c
@@ -2452,6 +2452,7 @@ static int decode_chunks(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *picture,
                     if (s2->pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_B) {
                         if (!s->closed_gop) {
                             skip_frame = 1;
+                            av_buffer_unref(&s->a53_buf_ref);
                             av_log(s2->avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG,
                                    "Skipping B slice due to open GOP\n");
                             break;
@@ -2465,6 +2466,7 @@ static int decode_chunks(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *picture,
                      * we have an invalid header. */
                     if (s2->pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_P && !s->sync) {
                         skip_frame = 1;
+                        av_buffer_unref(&s->a53_buf_ref);
                         av_log(s2->avctx, AV_LOG_DEBUG,
                                "Skipping P slice due to !sync\n");
                         break;
@@ -2476,6 +2478,7 @@ static int decode_chunks(AVCodecContext *avctx, AVFrame *picture,
                      s2->pict_type != AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I) ||
                     avctx->skip_frame >= AVDISCARD_ALL) {
                     skip_frame = 1;
+                    av_buffer_unref(&s->a53_buf_ref);
                     break;
                 }
 
